Z||000000||Frank R||04-13-2000||05:06 PM||||My car seems to have quite a few sales options.  The list has about 62 codes.  After spending some time in the parts and illustration book, only 14 options were found.  The list is long.  I need to find a reference to discover what the codes represent.  If posting the list of codes would be good, please advise.  Thanks for any guidance.  Frank R  in Idaho||||reg||6
Z||000001||theogre||04-13-2000||08:31 PM||||The RPO decal includes the entire configuration of the car as built, not just options. It doesn't include dealer options.<P>Alldata has the RPO codes in their database. If you have a local mechanic that gets this maybe they'll let you use it.<P>A dealer might also help.<P>You may have to use both to get a complete list.<P>Fastest way to read off the RPO decal is to read each column down and go from the left. Then you'll have them in sequential order same as they are listed by GM.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spyder||04-13-2000||08:46 PM||||Try this link: <A HREF="http://www.cjnetworks.com/~bott/options.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cjnetworks.com/~bott/options.html</A> <BR>I'm not sure if this is what you want.||||reg||1
